# B's diskette changed while its motor is off (roadmap disk-scheduler.md M8,
# D12): tests/posix/media.c (TEST_MEDIA_SWAPB) on MAME, whose Lua puts another
# diskette into B (media-at:). IBM's 360 KB drive has no change line, so the
# disk server checks B's first two sectors at the first access after 2 s of
# its silence: another diskette, the old one's cache dropped, the file it
# held gone; a file written on the new one and read back.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_MEDIA
define: TEST_MEDIA_SWAPB
emulators: mame
media-at: 75 eject B
media-at: 77 insert B other
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 600
---
media: B's readme.txt (bytes): {...}
media: B's readme.txt, another diskette (-2): -2
media: a file written on it (0): 0
media: read back (8): 8
media: done
